      "message": "Yeah, I looked at doing that a couple weeks ago in the hopes of creating a single vprintf-like function which can handle both format-to-string and format-to-uart.  So it\u0027d need to take a txchar() function which handles either output-to-uart or output-to-string.  But then for string output txchar needs to take a context pointer (to maintain the string position, so it doesn\u0027t rely on globals).  So it ends up looking like:\n\nint vprintf(int (*txchar)(int c, void *context), void *context, char *format, va_list args)\n\nThough now that\u0027s not looking as bad as it did before...  Maybe I\u0027ll code that up and see what it looks like.",
